                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb3d1b38-6b67-3999-91d8-915784bddf16",
                        "entry_id": "b457631c-043f-3439-ad03-4d6be9c7fd49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Développement de la musculature ou de certains groupes musculaires."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ae02924-a6bc-34f3-b6f8-63b4f847eddc",
                        "entry_id": "b457631c-043f-3439-ad03-4d6be9c7fd49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Culturisme, ensemble d'exercices spécialement étudiés pour favoriser ce développement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "648dd8aa-6f8f-4afb-a261-7ed293fb1da3",
                                "sense_id": "7ae02924-a6bc-34f3-b6f8-63b4f847eddc",
                                "text": "Aujourd’hui, quand les Français font du sport en dehors de leur domicile […] ils choisissent majoritairement de jouer au tennis […], ou bien ils participent à des séances de gymnastique, d’assouplissement, de musculation ou d’aérobic (9 % en 1985), ou bien encore ils nagent (8,6 % des interviewés joggent ou marathonent)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d23186cb-5531-473b-aedb-481030736f96",
                                "sense_id": "7ae02924-a6bc-34f3-b6f8-63b4f847eddc",
                                "text": "Dans un coin, de jeunes adolescents, torse nu, pratiquaient des exercices de musculation avec des haltères en ciment moulés dans des boîtes de conserve, d’autres étendus sur des nattes à l’ombre de l’arbre somnolaient ou sniffaient de la colle."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c71ef10-5bdf-4cf5-9441-72a50f1de81a",
                        "source_entry_id": "b457631c-043f-3439-ad03-4d6be9c7fd49",
                        "source_sense_id": "eb3d1b38-6b67-3999-91d8-915784bddf16",
                        "source_sense_description": "Développement de la musculature",
                        "target_lang_word": "musculation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "musculation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b55dc8e2-fb8c-381c-bec0-52e8329b8d79",
                                        "entry_id": "44598428-c8d0-37ac-982d-9e7f3be89ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The muscular system of an animal, or of any of its parts"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64cf3376-c198-4f1a-8ea9-11ef09182d03",
                                                "sense_id": "b55dc8e2-fb8c-381c-bec0-52e8329b8d79",
                                                "text": "This would not be the proper place for entering into an exhaustive account of the musculation of the Tyroglyphidæ; which would necessarily be lengthy , and would probably be of comparatively littel interest to most readers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2991a4ad-b561-4aab-9b9e-783dba7e1376",
                                                "sense_id": "b55dc8e2-fb8c-381c-bec0-52e8329b8d79",
                                                "text": "The main difference of it from Sokolov's scheme is the presence of dermal musculation and the specific features of the outer layers' structure,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                                        "entry_id": "44598428-c8d0-37ac-982d-9e7f3be89ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The use of muscles; muscular activity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eca87f4a-98c1-426a-a0c9-d98879bccbe0",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                                                "text": "Will has two provinces, musculaltion and attention."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d415fc5c-5a3b-45d1-abd2-225768118be8",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                                                "text": "For the muscle elements, being thus sustained by electrical force, and operated by electrical force, friction and strain during musculation are made impossible, a perpetual balance in force, which it necessarily involves, making it impossible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45ab27bc-29fb-494f-a0a8-82d42a503682",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                                                "text": "Whatever may be the remote causes of vocal defects, the direct cause is always a faulty musculation in the vocal mechanism. The method of training hitherto used to correct this faulty musculation has been for the most part an indirect one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c69f8a0-50b9-4a3b-911b-967ffbef6ddf",
                        "source_entry_id": "b457631c-043f-3439-ad03-4d6be9c7fd49",
                        "source_sense_id": "eb3d1b38-6b67-3999-91d8-915784bddf16",
                        "source_sense_description": "Développement de la musculature",
                        "target_lang_word": "muscolazione",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b41d630d-81ec-405f-95b7-ffd7bdb58953",
                        "source_entry_id": "b457631c-043f-3439-ad03-4d6be9c7fd49",
                        "source_sense_id": "7ae02924-a6bc-34f3-b6f8-63b4f847eddc",
                        "source_sense_description": "Culturisme",
                        "target_lang_word": "strength training",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "strength training",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31943347-04b4-3b1b-872c-b1c59bba0e5a",
                                        "entry_id": "da367b36-b16e-378a-bca7-1ca91ef2c642",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of exercise in which the goal is to increase the strength of muscles through low numbers of repetitions of an exercise performed with high resistance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ce57fc8-2d5b-4a97-bb1c-1e8c62bc75b8",
                                                "sense_id": "31943347-04b4-3b1b-872c-b1c59bba0e5a",
                                                "text": "Research and experience from major projects at Colorado State University and the United States Military Academy at West Point, and ongoing work at Nautilus headquarters in Lake Helen, Florida, support the concept that optimal strength training requires as little as one set of eight to twelve repetitions taken to momentary muscular failure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20243583-15d3-459d-8793-36e45cb5fae5",
                                                "sense_id": "31943347-04b4-3b1b-872c-b1c59bba0e5a",
                                                "text": "Unfortunately, many athletes […] shy away from true strength training programs with high intensities and lower repetitions because they fear \"bulking up\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6373e195-ceb8-4495-a5b7-8a35bb2aa3bb",
                                                "sense_id": "31943347-04b4-3b1b-872c-b1c59bba0e5a",
                                                "text": "Many strength training professionals prefer free-weight exercises."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "284a22c0-fea2-49d6-ae1c-4214376a3ee3",
                                                "sense_id": "31943347-04b4-3b1b-872c-b1c59bba0e5a",
                                                "text": "Although weightlifting is a sport in its own right, the techniques of the clean and jerk and the snatch are used extensively within sport-specific strength training and conditioning, as well as in more general strength training, due to their unparalleled ability to develop an individual's power."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
